Suggests: speech-dispatcher,
Description: car navigation for VibeOS
 Navi gives turn-by-turn directions for driving: a vector map from VibeOS's
 map server, routes with lanes, speed limits and speed cameras, spoken
 prompts, search with a microphone, saved places, and a reminder to leave.
 .
 MapLibre Native, which draws the map, is built into Navi's own library in
 /usr/lib/vibeos-navi, next to the libvibeos Navi was built with; no system
 library is replaced (libvibeos-1-0 still provides its settings schema).
 .
 The prompts are spoken with Agent's Piper voices, found in
 vibeos-dictate/voices/LANGUAGE under the user's or the system's data
 directories, and through Speech Dispatcher where there is none. The search's
 microphone uses vibeos-dictate's speech models.
